# Pipeline Structure Rules

- All user-facing entry points live in `scripts/` and accept a `--config` flag.
- All reusable logic lives in `src/` as importable Python modules.
- Every pipeline step must save its output artifact to disk before the next
  step begins. Never pass intermediate state only in memory across phase
  boundaries.
- Results must be reproducible from the same `seed + config + data`.
- Use `src.utils.logger.get_logger(__name__)` in every module.
- Every saved artifact must be logged with its full path at `INFO` level
  immediately after saving.
- Never reintroduce removed phases (e.g. registration, manual patch
  extraction); the architecture is dual-track radiomics + 3D SwinViT with
  cross-attention fusion.
